  },
  "packaging": "Two collectors approach the chassis from opposite sides. They feed a constrained serpentine path and a fixed-yaw launcher rather than a deep open bulk hopper. The launcher structure occupies one end of the base, while the four-bar links occupy side deployment space. The binder base image shows four corner drive modules and a lightened pan. Electronics under the pan require turning the robot over and removing its protective belly sheet according to the team release; do not draw those electronics as accessible through the ball path. Battery removal direction is not established. A fixed launcher can aim with the chassis while the side collectors sweep laterally, but that is a control and route advantage, not unrestricted acquisition in every heading.",
  "piece_flow": "Fuel meets either powered collector, crosses its bumper-side transition, enters the constrained conveyor, follows successive direction changes and reaches the feeder/variable-hood launcher. The exact merge of the two intake streams into the serpentine is not reconstructed by the isolated binder renders. Treat that merge as a critical unknown, not a straight connection invented in CAD.",
  "whole_robot_unknowns": [
    "The dual-inlet merge is the largest missing interface.",
    "Battery location, complete power routing, deployed dimensions and exact event chronology are unknown."
  ]
