  "packaging": "The rebuild uses a single front slapdown collector, an expanding storage enclosure over an inclined roller floor, and a full-width raised shooter at the opposite end. Corner swerve modules sit below this path; the launcher side structure carries the drum and hood and attaches down toward the drive rails. Source dimensions give a 27.5 by 27-inch frame. The hopper panels and their joints surround the ball path, so screw heads on the hood can rub a sliding wall. A source reply specifically explains using flathead screws there. Some electronics moved above the brainpan, but under-pan equipment still needs underside access. Preserve that service split. Do not infer battery removal without its source view.",
  "piece_flow": "The front collector lifts fuel across the bumper into the expanded hopper. Ten inclined rollers keep a broad stream moving toward the feeder. The backing panel returns piled fuel toward the shooter entry instead of allowing it to remain above the active floor. Feeder contacts lift and accelerate the stream; drum and powered hood contacts launch it. The full path must preserve width, not merely have a wide drum at the end. The same intake motion deploys storage, so acquisition and containment are mechanically coupled.",
