  "packaging": "A front collector and horizontally sliding wall feed a broad floor inside a square drivebase. The launcher stands across the rear; the floor hinges upward from its rear attachment to expose the electrical bay beneath. Intake-end floor supports rest on module-mounted hard stops and a retaining pin prevents unintended lifting. The hopper grows horizontally with the intake and vertically with a climber-linked upper enclosure. The whole render establishes the front-to-rear arrangement but does not establish every swept clearance. The battery and electronics are low, below the transport floor; the inspected electrical render shows component placement with the floor removed, not a complete battery-change sequence.",
  "piece_flow": "Fuel enters the front rollers, passes over the collector pivot and onto a floor with tube rollers and flex-wheel rollers. The floor feeds a curved tunnel, which turns travel upward toward the drum. Feeder, accelerating backing contacts, drum and hood share responsibility for the final entry state. The earlier interview calls the later path J-shaped and reports abandoning an S path; the new page is a separate publication snapshot. It names a different drum material from the retained interview, so do not fuse both descriptions into one certified build.",
